 739:     print("  -> %s" % v)
 740:     # FOUR STATES, FOUR EXIT CODES, because a caller that maps three of them onto
 741:     # "PASS" cannot report what it measured. 0 PASS, 1 FAIL, 2 UNCHECKABLE (ran,
 742:     # could not see -- not a pass), 3 WITHDRAWN (the definitions disagree AND no
 743:     # estimate is displayed, so the property is met by the withholding). A
 744:     # distinct CODE rather than a word in the output, so no caller has to
 745:     # substring-search for it -- which is the over-match this repository has now
 746:     # committed three times.
 747:     return {"PASS": 0, "FAIL": 1, "UNCHECKABLE": 2, "WITHDRAWN": 3}.get(v, 1)
